# Intent: with no link to Home, the unit nods and dances to music by itself (owner 2026-11-13: "when its offline, it could still listen to music and dance, right?"). While the hub link is down and the music features switch is on, each second's features go through the plain C judge (maipai_music_judge.h, tested equal to the host's Python judge) and its session machine: four seconds of music is the nod (the happy face), twenty seconds later the firmware dance, nine seconds without music ends it, two minutes between dances, six an hour, ten a day. Not while muted, in full quiet, listening, speaking, or on battery below 20 percent (a dance needs 40). While the link is up nothing here acts: the host decides. The nod is the face only on the unit (the host's head nod has no unit-side form yet).
# Upstream: MaiPai only (hal_music.cpp, hal_mcp.cpp). Applies after 120.
# Check after a flash: stop the hub, enable Dance to music before that, play a song: the happy face after about 5 s, the dance after about 25 s; serial lines "offline music: nod / dance / end"; start the hub: a running dance stops.
